+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Window: display.ini, aspect-correct presentation, borderless fullscreen
+ *
+ * The swap chain is the guest's display surface and stays at the guest size
+ * (1280x720): draws to display offset 0, the display-buffer copy at present
+ * and every readback (CELLMARK_DUMP, RSX_CAP) depend on that, so it is never
+ * resized. It belongs to a child window -- the "view" -- and
+ * DXGI_SCALING_STRETCH maps it onto the view's client area. The view is laid
+ * out as the largest rectangle of the content aspect centred in the
+ * top-level window's client area; the rest is the window class's black
+ * background (letterbox / pillarbox bars). Resizing, maximising, fullscreen
+ * and DPI changes therefore only move the view: SetWindowPos on a child of
+ * this thread's own window, synchronous, with no GPU wait and no
+ * ResizeBuffers. All of it runs in the window procedure on the window
+ * thread, which is also the render thread (between frames, from
+ * rsx_d3d12_backend_pump_messages, or nested in a SetWindowPos this file
+ * makes), so it never races a frame.
+ *
+ * The view is disabled and transparent to hit-testing: every mouse and
+ * keyboard message still goes to the top-level window, whose procedure
+ * hands them to cellPad first, and cellPad's capture clips the cursor to
+ * the top-level client area and re-clips on WM_SIZE / WM_MOVE.
+ *
+ * present = stretch (display.ini) puts the swap chain on the top-level
+ * window itself instead: the old behaviour, stretched to whatever shape the
+ * window has.
+ *
+ * The menu bar (File / Save / Load / View, rsx_winmenu.c; menu_bar = 0 turns
+ * it off) is non-client area: the window is created with it and its height
+ * added to the frame, so the client area and the picture are the size they
+ * were without it. Borderless fullscreen takes it off and puts it back.
+ * -----------------------------------------------------------------------*/
+
