+ * With two FLIP_DISCARD buffers the back buffer handed out after a vsync'd
+ * Present is the one still on screen, and a command list that references it
+ * does not start on the GPU until the next vblank has flipped the new frame in
+ * (measured here: a list holding only that buffer's barrier, submitted 2 ms
+ * after Present(1), completes 10.5 ms later at 74 Hz; one that does not touch
+ * it, 0.05 ms). Every render_frame batch transitions, binds and clears the back
