+/* Pack/unpack (RPCS3 FragmentProgramDecompiler handle_sct_scb/handle_tex_srb,
+ * after NV_fragment_program): a pack writes the 32-bit packed word, as float
+ * bits, to every component (the write mask picks .x in practice); an unpack
+ * reads .x's bits. PKB/UPB = 4 x unorm8 (x in the low byte), PK4/UP4 = 4 x
+ * snorm8, PK2/UP2 = 2 x fp16, PK16/UP16 = 2 x unorm16, PKG = linear->sRGB
+ * then PKB, UPG = UPB then sRGB->linear (all four channels, as RPCS3).
+ * inFamous 2's G-buffer materials end on PKG R0.x, H4 ; UPB H0.xyz, R0 -- its
+ * albedo leaves through these two. Unhandled, h0 kept whatever it last held
