+ * rsx_ztex compares each texel of the 2x2 footprint with the coordinate's r
+ * (z, or z/w for TXP; clamped to [0,1]) by the unit's ZFUNC, then filters the
+ * results (PCF) or takes the nearest; ZFUNC 0 returns the (filtered) depth
+ * itself. Its control
+ * byte in fp_texctl is ZFUNC (bits 0-2) | linear (bit 3) | footprint (bits
+ * 5-6: 0 exact, 1 the old gather-at-uv, 2 diagnostic diff) instead of the
+ * expand/gamma bits (the byte is the same at every rsx_fp_set_shadow_filter setting; that setting only swaps the
+ * kernel the decompiled helper applies). A SIGNED unit's byte marks a signed channel by setting
+ * both its expand and its gamma bit, a combination that cannot otherwise
+ * occur. Cube units are never DEPTH. */
+#define RSX_FP_TEX_NORMAL        0u
+#define RSX_FP_TEX_DEPTH_PACKED  1u
+#define RSX_FP_TEX_DEPTH         2u
+#define RSX_FP_TEX_SIGNED        3u
+void rsx_fp_set_tex_modes(u32 modes);
