+/* ===========================================================================
+ * SAVE STATES (M4b; engine design 4.2, 5.2, 6.2): the KOBJ and KMEM sections
+ * and the system clock's TIME anchor.
+ *
+ * Both sections gather state that several files own. This file is linked
+ * into every program that runs a guest, and the runtime library's files may
+ * not call into it, so it holds the two sections and calls the others' parts.
+ *
+ * KOBJ, the lv2 objects (restore order SS_ORDER_KERNEL)
+ *   queues, events, ports, eflags   sys_event.c (sys_event_ss_capture)
+ *   semaphores        sys_semaphore.c: the value only, never the waiters
+ *   lwmutexes         this file's registry, by guest address: whether its host
+ *                     semaphore is taken now (probed: taken if free, given
+ *                     straight back), and the guest owner / recursion words
+ *                     (no-restore: GMEM restores them; M4c checks the two
+ *                     agree before it takes the semaphore as the owner)
+ *   lwconds           this file's registry, by guest address: the waiters
+ *                     registered and the tokens signals left in the host
+ *                     semaphore (drained, counted, given back) -- an exact
+ *                     lwcond resume needs both (critique B2)
+ *   lwcond_waits      per guest thread inside sys_lwcond_wait (keyed by tid,
+ *                     to pair with its PPUT park): the lwcond, its mutex, the
+ *                     owner / recursion it released and will write back, the
+ *                     return code a timed-out wait will give, and the phase
+ *                     (1 waiting for a signal, 2 re-taking the mutex)
+ *   asserted_empty    sys_mutex, sys_cond, sys_rwlock, sys_timer, the
+ *                     interrupt-thread bindings, sys_vm mappings and the HLE
+ *                     cellSpurs tables: the title uses none, so none is
+ *                     saved, check() refuses while one is live, and these
+ *                     counts (all 0) record that in the image
+ * KMEM, the allocators (restore order SS_ORDER_ALLOC)
+ *   allocations, containers, shared, sys_memory   sys_memory.c
+ *   sys_vm            sys_vm.c: the sys_vm window's bump (unmapping never
+ *                     rewinds it, so it is saved with no mapping live)
+ *   loader            ppu_loader.cpp: the mmapper VA bumps, the TLS-block
+ *                     bump, the OPD fixups
+ *   sysprx            this file: the CRT TLS bump, the mmapper ids and sizes,
+ *                     the gcm scratch bump, the lwcond id, the SPU segment
+ *                     bump and image records, the net fd and errno cell
+ *   stacks            sys_ppu_thread.c's g_vm_stack_alloc (guest stacks)
+ * TIME anchor "sys_time.system_us": what sys_time_get_system_time reports now
+ * (0: never read); M4c re-anchors s_systime_base from it (design 6.4).
+ *
+ * Everything runs with every guest thread, SPU thread and the mixer parked:
+ * plain reads, no lock, no allocation. Probing a host semaphore with a
+ * zero-timeout wait and giving the token back takes no lock either, and with
+ * everything parked nobody can take or post one in between.
+ *
+ * THE LOAD (M4c; ss_state.h "THE LOAD", engine design 6.2). No guest thread
+ * exists when teardown and restore run, so every host object of the old
+ * state is free to close, and every one the image needs is made anew.
+ *   KOBJ teardown  the lv2 tables of the files that own them, timers first
+ *                  (a timer thread posts to queues): each live object's
+ *                  handles and locks closed, the tables empty; then EVERY
+ *                  slot of the lwmutex / lwcond registries (critique H8: a
+ *                  slot left with its old count would hand it to a later
+ *                  object at that address) and the lwcond wait records.
+ *   KOBJ restore   the objects at their ids, rings at head 0, waiter counts
+ *                  0 (the resumed waits count themselves again); each
+ *                  lwmutex's semaphore created taken if it was taken -- GMEM
